      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<line-height=45>Painted in 1889, The Bedroom depicts Vincent van Gogh''s
    room in the Yellow House in Arles, southern France. Its unusual perspective,
    simplified forms, and expressive colors transform an ordinary interior into a
    deeply personal space.

    Van Gogh wanted the painting to communicate a sense
    of rest and tranquility. Yet the tilted furniture, strong outlines, and contrasting
    colors create a distinctive visual tension.

    Rather than reproducing the
    room exactly as it appeared, he used color and composition to express how the
    space felt to him.

    Look closer: Notice how the angled floorboards, bright
    walls, and carefully arranged furniture shape your experience of the room.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7bacdcbe9e0a54868b3dab2876c83339, type: 2}
